# Asset contract: what the game loads from `assets/`

Owner of `assets/`: `artist` (assignment.json in `world/producer`). Owner of this list and of the loader: `game-developer`.
This answers `game-developer`#3. The game reads **only** `assets/manifest.json` and the files it names; every name below is a key the code looks up.

## General rules

- Logical screen 256×240, 16×16 tile grid. PNG, 1× native pixel size, transparent background (alpha 0), NES-like palette. The game draws with nearest-neighbour scaling.
- **Facing:** Mario frames face **right**; enemy frames face **left** (their starting walk direction). The game mirrors horizontally as needed; Podoboo and dead enemies are flipped vertically by the game.
- **Anchor:** the game places every character/item frame by its **bottom-centre**. A frame's rect is its full cell; draw the figure inside it, standing on the cell's bottom row unless noted.
- Animation timing belongs to the game (it is gameplay: e.g. Mario's walk cycle speed follows his speed). `anims` in the manifest are allowed but ignored; supply the frames.
- A frame name the game asks for that is missing is drawn as a magenta box and listed with `console.warn` + the `?debug=1` overlay, so gaps are visible to QA. Extra frames are ignored.

## `assets/manifest.json` shape

```json
{
  "manifest_schema": 1,
  "sheets": {
    "player":  { "file": "sprites/player.png",  "frames": { "small_idle": [0, 0, 16, 16] } },
    "enemies": { "file": "sprites/enemies.png", "frames": { "goomba_walk1": [0, 0, 16, 16] },
                 "variants": { "underground": "sprites/enemies_underground.png", "castle": "sprites/enemies_castle.png" } },
    "items":   { "file": "sprites/items.png",   "frames": { } },
    "tiles":   { "file": "tiles/overworld.png", "frames": { },
                 "variants": { "underground": "tiles/underground.png", "underwater": "tiles/underwater.png",
                               "castle": "tiles/castle.png", "snow": "tiles/snow.png" } },
    "scenery": { "file": "tiles/scenery.png",   "frames": { },
                 "variants": { "snow": "tiles/scenery_snow.png" } }
  },
  "font":  { "file": "ui/font.png", "cell": [8, 8], "columns": 16, "chars": "0123456789ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ-x!.,'?©" },
  "title": { "file": "ui/title.png" },
  "palette": { "sky_day": "#5c94fc", "sky_night": "#000000", "underground": "#000000", "castle": "#000000", "underwater": "#2038ec" },
  "audio": {
    "jump_small": { "file": "audio/sfx/jump_small.ogg" },
    "overworld":  { "files": ["audio/music/overworld.ogg", "audio/music/overworld.mp3"], "loop": true, "loopStart": 0.0, "loopEnd": 0.0 }
  }
}
```

- `variants`: a theme key → another PNG with **identical frame names and rects**; the game swaps the image by theme. A theme without a variant uses the base file. Theme keys: `overworld` (base), `underground`, `underwater`, `castle`, `snow` (the pale "winter" palette of 5-1/5-2/7-1/3-1/3-2/6-3); night levels use the base tiles with the `sky_night` colour.
- `font`: glyph `chars[i]` is at cell `(i % columns, floor(i / columns))`. `x` is the multiplication sign in `x 03`. `©` optional.
- `palette`: background fill colours (sky). Optional; the values above are the defaults.
- `audio`: `file` or `files` (first one the browser can play is used; one OGG is enough for Chrome/Firefox). `loop: true` for music; `loopStart`/`loopEnd` in seconds (omit or `loopEnd: 0` = loop whole file). Optional `volume` 0–1.

## Frames

Sizes are w×h in pixels. "P0" = needed for World 1-1 (first milestone); "P1" = World 1; "P2" = Worlds 2–8.

### `player` — Mario (P0 unless noted)

| frames | size | note |
|---|---|---|
| `small_idle`, `small_walk1`, `small_walk2`, `small_walk3`, `small_skid`, `small_jump`, `small_die` | 16×16 | `small_die` faces the viewer |
| `small_climb1`, `small_climb2` | 16×16 | flagpole / vine, facing right, pole on his right |
| `small_swim1` … `small_swim4` | 16×16 | P2 (underwater) |
| `big_idle`, `big_walk1`, `big_walk2`, `big_walk3`, `big_skid`, `big_jump`, `big_crouch` | 16×32 | crouch drawn in the bottom of the cell |
| `big_climb1`, `big_climb2` | 16×32 | |
| `big_swim1` … `big_swim4` | 16×32 | P2 |
| `big_grow` | 16×32 | the half-size frame shown in the grow/shrink flicker |
| `fire_*` | 16×32 | same names as every `big_*` frame (fire palette), plus `fire_throw` |

Star invincibility: optional `star1_*`, `star2_*`, `star3_*` copies of the `small_*`/`big_*` frames in the 3 flashing palettes. If absent the game tints the frames itself.

