### UI

- `ui/font.png`: 8×8 glyphs, white on transparent (the game draws HUD text white; the title uses the same font). P0.
- `ui/title.png`: the title board ("SUPER MARIO BROS." sign), about 176×88. P0. Don't draw a Nintendo copyright line.

## Audio ids

Music (`loop: true`): `overworld`, `underground`, `underwater`, `castle`, `star` (P0: overworld, underground, star). Hurry-up versions `overworld_hurry`, `underground_hurry`, `underwater_hurry`, `castle_hurry` (faster); if a hurry version is absent the game plays the normal one.

Jingles (play once): `warning` (hurry-up jingle at TIME 100), `stage_clear` (after the flagpole), `castle_clear` (after the axe), `death`, `gameover`, `ending` (princess), `pipe_intro` (P1, the short walk-into-pipe tune of x-2 openings, optional).

Sound effects: `jump_small`, `jump_big`, `coin`, `stomp`, `kick`, `bump`, `brick_break`, `powerup_appear`, `powerup`, `powerdown` (damage and pipe travel), `oneup`, `fireball`, `flagpole`, `firework`, `beep` (time-bonus tally tick), `pause`, `vine` (P1), `bowser_fire` (P1), `bowser_fall` (P1), `cannon` (P2), `swim` (P2, falls back to `stomp`).

## Where the game reads them

`src/assets.js` loads the manifest, the PNGs and the audio; `src/` code refers only to the names above. Run `?debug=1` to see the missing-asset list on screen.
